  "decision_conditions": [
    "The use of the first and second floors of the site as a house in multiple occupation is hereby granted for a temporary period of a maximum of two years from the date of this permission.  The use shall cease within two years of the granting of the permission and the first and second floor returned to ancillary residential accommodation, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To allow the Local Planning Authority to monitor the prevailing circumstances at the site and to have effective control.",
    "The use shall be completed in accordance with the following approved drawings and maintained thereafter to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority:\r\rBlock plan Location plan DRG No 100 Sept '25\rProposed Block plan DRG No 200 Sept '25\rProposed Ground floor plan DRG No 210 Sept '25\rProposed First floor plan DRG No 211 Sept '25\rProposed Second floor plan DRG No 212 Sept '25\r Proposed Roof plan DRG No 213 Sept '25\rSupporting Statement September 2025  \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "Within three months of the date of the permission hereby granted, a comprehensive Flood Management Plan, which includes a distinct evacuation route located in the Very Low Hazard Level according to FD2320, as well as an indication of refuge areas during a storm event, shall be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details. \r\rReason: To ensure that all occupants and visitors to the property can be safely evacuated in the event of a flooding event\r",
    "Within three months of the date of the permission hereby granted, full details of the roof terraces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority and implemented. The use shall be completed in accordance with the approved details and maintained thereafter to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To provide satisfactory outdoor amenity space for occupants.",
    "Within three months of the date of this permission, unless otherwise agreed by the Local Planning Authority, revised drawings showing \r cycle parking must be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of TEN long stay cycle parking spaces and two short stay spaces in a separate location (i.e not within the locked enclosure)\r\r- In an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\r\r- Secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\r\r- Fully enclosed: four walls and a roof\r\rThe use must be completed in accordance with the approved details, within three months of the date of the permission.\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.",
    "Within three months of the date of this permission, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority, a detailed waste strategy for the storage and collection of refuse and recycling from the site shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The use shall operate in accordance with the approved details.\r\r Reason:  To ensure that all waste is properly stored and removed from site.",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 16 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen, lounge and bathroom shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
